WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.950
Here's a cartoon cat.

2
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:03.030
Zoom in.

3
00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:04.150
Closer.

4
00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:05.690
Closer still.

5
00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:09.730
Suddenly the cat falls apart
into tiny coloured squares.

6
00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:12.290
In an image editor, you double the width,

7
00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:13.810
and double the height.

8
00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:15.730
The new file size is hidden.

9
00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:18.390
So how much bigger will the file be?

10
00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:22.270
In this mission, you'll see that
a bitmap is a grid of pixels,

11
00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:24.230
short for picture elements.

12
00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:27.530
You'll describe an image as
width by height in pixels,

13
00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:30.570
and see why more pixels means more detail.

14
00:00:30.620 --> 00:00:35.750
And you'll meet colour depth: the number
of bits used to store each pixel's colour.

15
00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:40.170
Your mission: work out how much bigger
the file gets when you double a photo's

16
00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:41.280
width and height.
